WSJT-X is a separate work, not included here. It is available from
https://wsjt.sourceforge.io/ and is published under the GNU General Public
License.

This program does not link any WSJT-X code. The shim is an independent dylib
that macOS loads into the process at run time through DYLD_INSERT_LIBRARIES,
and it replaces only documented libSystem clock entry points - gettimeofday,
clock_gettime, clock_gettime_nsec_np, time and the mach_*_time family.

`timeshift-resign` does not redistribute WSJT-X either. It duplicates the copy
already installed on your own machine and re-signs that duplicate with your own
signing identity, so that macOS will honour DYLD_INSERT_LIBRARIES for it. The
duplicate never leaves your machine, and your original installation is left
untouched.
